### verdict ###
  any klein counterexample inside THM-1032's stratum: False
  => THM-1032 UNAFFECTED (its stratum and klein's danger zone are DISJOINT)

### where does the danger actually live?  gap-ratio profile ###
  set                              maxratio  dominant-killer?  M          1/(n-1)
  [1, 3, 4, 5, 7, 11, 18, 32]      32        False             4/33       1/8   (M<1/(n-1): True)
  [1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 30]     30        False             4/37       1/9   (M<1/(n-1): True)

--- RUN NOTE (kind-pasteur, honest) ---
The final M_of() row (n=11 set) was CUT by the 560s timeout: M_of scans all a/q with
q <= 4000, which is ~8M rational reductions per set and the n=11 set has 10 speeds.
The VERDICT section above completed and is unaffected -- it uses only the ratio tests,
which are exact integer comparisons.  The two M values that did print (4/33 < 1/8 and
4/37 < 1/9) independently reproduce klein-S321's reported values.
The n=11 set [2,6,8,9,10,11,13,14,17,19] has max ratio 19/2 = 9.5 < 13, so it is not
even GapFamily -- it is a purely compressed object and lies outside the trapped core
as well as outside THM-1032's stratum.
